{
  "problem": {
    "title": "Noble Estate Inheritance Partition",
    "description": "A noble's estate (183000 total value) must be split between two sons. 14 items: painting=25000, bust=5000, vase=20000, porsche=40000, diamond1=12000, diamond2=12000, diamond3=12000, sofa=3000, dog1=3000, dog2=3000, sculpture=10000, boat=15000, harley=10000, furniture=13000. Binary assign[i]=1 means item goes to son2. Dogs must stay together: assign[dog1]=assign[dog2]. Minimize the absolute difference |son2_value - son1_value|.",
    "problem_type": "mixed_integer_programming",
    "objective": "minimize",
    "objective_description": "Absolute difference between the two sons' shares = |2*sum(value*assign) - 183000|",
    "constraints": [
      {
        "description": "Dogs must stay together: assign[dog1] - assign[dog2] = 0"
      },
      {
        "description": "diff >= son2_value - son1_value: diff - 2*sum(value*assign) >= -183000"
      },
      {
        "description": "diff >= son1_value - son2_value: diff + 2*sum(value*assign) >= 183000"
      }
    ],
    "decision_variables": [
      "assign[i]: binary, 1 if item i goes to son2 (0 = son1)",
      "diff: scalar continuous (lb=0), the absolute value of (son2_total - son1_total)"
    ],
    "parameters": [
      "value[i]: monetary value of item i"
    ],
    "additional_notes": "Total estate = 183000. son2_value = sum(value[i]*assign[i]). son1_value = 183000 - son2_value. |son2-son1| = |2*son2_value - 183000|. Linearised with diff scalar: diff >= 2*son2 - 183000 and diff >= 183000 - 2*son2. Optimal obj=1000 (son2=92000, son1=91000). Two scalar constraints (domain=[]) use indexed_sum over Items. dog_link constraint (domain=[]) uses hardcoded member IDs 'dog1','dog2'.",
    "csv_file_paths": {
      "items": "items.csv"
    }
  },
